@scene chapter_3_endless_bridge

background: forest_gate.png
music: mystery_forest.mp3

dialogue:
"Beyond the Echoing Halls the forest thins, and the path simply... stops."

background: valley_vista.jpg

dialogue:
"The ground falls away into a chasm so deep its bottom is only a rumour."
"On the far side, half-lost in mist, the path resumes. Between them: nothing."
"Only a weathered pillar at the cliff's lip, carved with instructions worn almost smooth."

npc You:
"There's no way across."

dialogue:
"As you speak, the air near the pillar curdles."
"A stain the colour of a healed-over wound clings to the stone — the same wrongness the System has warned of."
"The Blight. Where it touches, things forget how to work."
"Here, it has devoured the bridge itself."

system notification:
"NEW QUEST"
"THE ENDLESS BRIDGE"
"Build a path across the Blighted chasm."

dialogue:
"The Warden reaches the cliff's lip ahead of you, looks down, and for the first time since you met him, stands perfectly still."
"'An age of walking,' he says, 'and the one stretch I never had to cross was the one that isn't there.'"

npc System:
"The bridge was not broken, Traveller. It was UNMADE. It has forgotten how to repeat itself."
"A bridge is only one plank — laid again, and again, until it reaches the other side."

dialogue:
"The pillar's carvings flare to life."

npc System:
"You know the shape of this, Traveller. A count, and a body that runs once for every number in it."
"Each plank must reach further than the last: the first spans one length, the second two, the third three."
"Total them, and the crossing is paid for."

system system:
"MISSION"
"Loop from 1 to n, adding each number to span."

mission: loops_intro

background: valley_vista.jpg

dialogue:
"You speak the loop. A plank of light snaps into being, then another on its echo, then a third."
"The bridge unrolls across the chasm, one plank per count, until it kisses the far edge. You cross."

background: deep_forest.jpg

dialogue:
"The Warden crosses behind you, slowly, testing every plank with his boot as though he still cannot believe a thing can end."

background: warden

npc Warden:
"A count, and a plank for every number in it. That is my corridor, turned honest."
"I paced an age because I never gave my loop a place to STOP. You gave yours one before you laid a single board."
"Do that with every loop you write, traveller. Ask it where it ends before you ask it what it does."

dialogue:
"He turns north, whistling something tuneless, and is gone into the trees."
"The road ahead runs east — and somewhere along it, a great deal of shouting is going on."

system level_up:
"CHAPTER COMPLETE"
"The Endless Bridge"
"Applied: for loops · range · a running total"

reward:
xp: 100
gold: 40
achievement: BRIDGE-BUILDER

next:
chapter_4b_satchel_of_slots
